# Thought Reflection: "If you would draw a card, draw two cards instead" (CR 121.6, 614.1a). Bot1 casts it on turn 1. In its
# turn 3 draw step the draw for the turn is replaced by two (the effect has no exception for the draw step), and Ancestral
# Recall's three draws are each replaced on their own (CR 121.2, the card's ruling: "Draw three" draws six), so Bot1 draws
# eight cards in all: its hand is the Ancestral Recall left from turn 1, the two of the draw step less the Island played,
# and six more; the library loses eight of its twenty Islands. Without the effect it would hold three and keep sixteen.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Thought Reflection
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

